<p>Zaragoza Airport operates a single, compact passenger terminal, so there's no confusion over where to head once you arrive, unlike the larger multi-terminal airports in Madrid or Barcelona. The airport is internationally notable chiefly for cargo rather than passenger numbers — the adjacent PLAZA logistics platform makes ZAZ Spain's second-busiest cargo airport after Madrid-Barajas — but that freight traffic runs entirely separately from the passenger side, keeping check-in and security quick. Your driver drops you at the terminal front, comfortably within the 20-minute window from the hotel.</p>
